      "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_doubt_science",
      "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: 'Doubt science & established historical records?'",
      "description": "The text 'doubt science & established historical records?' is used to imply that the Black man is ignorant or irrational, which is a direct reference to the anti-Black stereotype that Black people are less capable of understanding or accepting scientific facts or historical truths. This stereotype is used to demean and dehumanize the individual based on his race.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3d32d208"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_036cb184",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "meme_composition_juxtaposition",
      "label": "Meme Composition: Juxtaposition of racial stereotypes",
      "description": "The meme's overall intent relies on the juxtaposition of two images: a person in Native American regalia (often stereotyped as 'savage' or 'primitive') and a Black man in formal attire (often stereotyped as 'sophisticated' or 'refined'). This juxtaposition is used to create a hateful message that targets the Black man based on his race, implying that he is inferior or irrational. The use of the Native American image as a 'primitive' reference is a real-world reference to the historical stereotype of Native Americans as 'savages' or 'uncivilized'.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3d32d208"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
